## Checking it

`validate` reproduces each `reference/` fixture on this machine. Those fixtures
were written by the **trained torch model** at export time, not by these
graphs, so a pass covers the whole chain: trained model, export, runtime,
platform. The tolerances are 1e-3 of each column's normalisation scale,
headroom for float differences between machines; the export itself agreed
with the trained model much more tightly (`agreement_at_export` in each
`REFERENCE.json`).
